latest_plan = 'Based on the reflection, here\'s a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the input grid:\n   a. Determine the dimensions of the input grid.\n   b. Identify the gray (5) dividing line.\n\n2. Extract vertical patterns:\n   a. Scan both sides of the dividing line for continuous vertical color patterns.\n   b. For each side, record the color and relative position of each vertical line.\n   c. Consider a line "continuous" if it spans at least half the height of the grid.\n\n3. Identify horizontal lines:\n   a. Scan each row of the input grid.\n   b. If a row contains a single color (excluding black and gray) across the entire width (ignoring the dividing line), mark it as a horizontal line.\n\n4. Create the output grid:\n   a. Initialize a 7-column grid with the same height as the input grid.\n   b. Fill all cells with black (0) initially.\n\n5. Map vertical patterns to the output grid:\n   a. Calculate the relative positions of vertical lines in the input grid.\n     - For lines left of the divider, calculate position as: column / divider_column\n     - For lines right of the divider, calculate position as: (column - divider_column - 1) / (total_columns - divider_column - 1)\n   b. Map these relative positions to the 7-column output grid:\n     - For each vertical line, calculate its output column as: round(relative_position * 6) + 1\n   c. If multiple lines map to the same column, adjust by moving them to the nearest empty column.\n   d. Apply the vertical lines to the output grid, ensuring they span from top to bottom.\n\n6. Apply horizontal lines:\n   a. For each horizontal line identified in step 3, fill the entire corresponding row in the output grid with the line\'s color.\n\n7. Ensure continuity of vertical patterns:\n   a. Scan each column of the output grid from top to bottom.\n   b. If a cell is black (0) and has the same non-black color above and below it, fill it with that color to ensure continuity.\n\n8. Handle intersections:\n   a. Where horizontal and vertical lines intersect, prioritize the horizontal line color.\n\n9. Final check:\n   a. Ensure all cells in the output grid have a valid color (0-9).\n   b. Verify that the output grid dimensions are correct (7 columns, same height as input).\n\nThis plan should provide a more general solution that can handle the various cases presented in the challenge. It preserves the relative positioning of vertical lines, maintains horizontal lines, and ensures continuity of patterns while fitting everything into the standardized 7-column output format.'
